    {
      "external_id": "C11-PHY-CH2-2.3-CHARACTERISTICS-OF-SCALAR-PRODUCT-RU",
      "chapter": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2",
      "topic": "pk-punjab/xi/physics/c11-phy/ch2/u-characteristics-of-scalar-product",
      "title": "Characteristics of Scalar Product (Roman Urdu)",
      "language": "roman_ur",
      "variant_of": "C11-PHY-CH2-2.3-CHARACTERISTICS-OF-SCALAR-PRODUCT",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "e2c5c034-041b-5340-9823-5e3c8c88a07c",
          "pdf_from": 25,
          "pdf_to": 25,
          "note": "Characteristics of Scalar Product: a main subheading of 2.3 Product of two vectors, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 25-25."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "1. A⃗.B⃗ = AB cos θ aur B⃗.A⃗ = BA cos θ = AB cos θ, is liye A⃗.B⃗ = B⃗.A⃗. Multiply karne ke order (tarteeb) se farq nahi parta; yani scalar product commutative (order badalne se jawab nahi badalta) hai."
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "2. Do perpendicular vectors (θ = 90°) ka scalar product zero hota hai, kyun ke cos 90° = 0."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{B} = AB\\cos 90^\\circ = 0",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.B⃗ = AB cos 90° = 0"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "3. Do parallel vectors ka scalar product un ki magnitudes ke product ke barabar hota hai. Parallel vectors (θ = 0°) ke liye cos 0° = 1:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{B} = AB\\cos 0^\\circ = AB",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.B⃗ = AB cos 0° = AB"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Antiparallel (ulti direction wale) vectors (θ = 180°) ke liye cos 180° = -1:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{B} = AB\\cos 180^\\circ = -AB",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.B⃗ = AB cos 180° = -AB"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Kisi vector A⃗ ka apne aap se scalar product (self product) us ki magnitude ke square ke barabar hota hai:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{A} = AA\\cos 0^\\circ = A^2",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.A⃗ = AA cos 0° = A²"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Rectangular components ke zariye do vectors A⃗ aur B⃗ ka scalar product:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{B} = A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z \\tag{2.7}",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.B⃗ = AxBx + AyBy + AzBz   (2.7)"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Equation (2.6) se do vectors ke darmiyan angle nikal sakte hain. Kyun ke"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\vec{A}\\cdot\\vec{B} = AB\\cos\\theta = A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z",
            "text_alt": "A⃗.B⃗ = AB cos θ = AxBx + AyBy + AzBz"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\text{Therefore}\\quad \\cos\\theta = \\frac{A_xB_x + A_yB_y + A_zB_z}{AB} \\tag{2.8}",
            "text_alt": "Therefore cos θ = (AxBx + AyBy + AzBz)/AB   (2.8)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
